      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The primary systemic vasculitides are heterogeneous, multisystem disorders characterized by inflammation and necrosis of small and medium blood vessels. Patients with antineutrophil cytoplasmic autoantibodies associated vasculitis have increased mortality rate as a consequence of cardiovascular disease. Measures to reduce the risk of cardiovascular disease should be integral to the management of systemic vasculitis. The preventive therapy for accelerated atherosclerosis in systemic vasculitis should be based on aggressive approach against inflammation and against risk factors of premature atherosclerosis such as hypertension, smoking, inactivity, obesity and unhealthy diet. All patients with antineutrophil cytoplasmic autoantibodies associated vasculitis should be subjected to prolonged follow-up at dedicated clinics and frequent screening for cardiovascular risk factors."},
